\subsection{Definitions and mathematical statement}
\paragraph{Statement recorded in the supplied source.}
For all positive m,n and every stationary integral m-varifold V in an open subset of $R^{m+n}$, is $dim_H$ $Sing(V)\leq m-1$? Sing(V) excludes points with a neighborhood on which V is a constant positive integer multiple of a smooth embedded minimal m-submanifold.

\subsection{Short English statement}
For all positive m,n and every stationary integral m-varifold V in an open subset of $R^{m+n}$, is $dim_H$ $Sing(V)\leq m-1$? Sing(V) excludes points with a neighborhood on which V is a constant positive integer multiple of a smooth embedded minimal m-submanifold.

\subsection{Sources}
\begin{itemize}
\item[S1] Original question source or mathematical context.
\url{https://arxiv.org/html/2503.00651}.
\item[S2] OpenAI, manuscript citation page. Source of the formulation motivating this local problem.
\url{https://github.com/openai/math/blob/adc7f1241b42e322a6451854ab7e4b4c146bf78a/preprints/A-Codimension-One-Bound-for-the-Singular-Set-of-a-Stationary-Integral-Varifold-October-5-2026/README.md}.
\end{itemize}

